A||||1||yellowTee||Jumps out of 5th gear||||4||
Z||000000||yellowTee||05-13-2001||10:11 PM||||I am hoping that someone can help me!  I own a 88 Formula, last night when I was coming home I went to put my car into 5th gear.  When I let the clutch out it jumped out of gear.  After trying it three times it finally stayed in.  Is there something I can look at, adjust or have to replace? I have only been on here for a short time but it seemed you guys would know the most.  Please help, I can't afford to replace the transmission.  Thanks in advance!!<P>------------------<BR>84 white 2m4<BR>88 yellow t-top, factory||||reg||4
Z||000001||mrfiero||05-13-2001||11:26 PM||||Check your fluid level!!  I'm betting that you're low......hopefully you haven't suffered any permanent damage.<BR> <BR>A friend of mine had this happen to him while driving up Vail pass (10K feet in elevation)......his axle seals were shot, he lost all of the fluid in the tranny and he locked it up (melted the "guts" together).  He said it popped out of gear while driving before it jammed in neutral.<P>If your fluid level is fine then you have some internal problem.....probably a bent or broken shift rail.  Check and adjust the fluid level first and let us know what you find out.<p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 05-13-2001).]||||reg||1
